  "title": "P300 dataset BI2014a from a \"Brain Invaders\" experiment",
  "description": "This dataset contains EEG recordings from 64 healthy participants playing Brain Invaders, a visual P300 brain-computer interface videogame based on an oddball paradigm with a grid of 36 symbols. Data were recorded with 16 dry electrodes at GIPSA-lab, Grenoble, in 2014 to study the viability of a calibration-less P300-based BCI. This is a BIDS-formatted derivative of the original Zenodo deposit, produced via MOABB.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 512 Hz from 16 dry gold-alloy g.Sahara electrodes with a g.USBamp amplifier (reference right earlobe, ground FZ) using OpenVibe. Participants played nine game levels, with up to eight attempts per level to destroy a target symbol. Each repetition had 12 flashes (2 target, 10 non-target), and a real-time adaptive Riemannian Minimum Distance to Mean classifier assessed the participants' commands.",
